Philip Potter schrieb:
> 
> hcobb wrote:
> > Having fire resistance shouldn't protect the thing's I'm wearing when
> > I poke a Fire Elemental with a wooden dagger while carrying a wooden
> > shield and wearing a non-fireproof robe.
> 
> Do fire elementals damage equipment if you're not fire resistant?
> Wizmode test suggests not.

Poking it and receiving the "backlash" fire damage doesn't hurt items. 
However, if a fire elemental hits you in melee and gets past your
magic cancellation, it _may_ set you on fire. This can damage
equipment and inventory; and it will do so regardless of the
character's fire resistance status.

